AgentsCode
==========

The interface is built from MonoCode's UI (https://github.com/hardbeat920/monocode).
MonoCode is a Tauri app whose frontend calls a Rust backend directly, so AgentsCode
vendors its portable primitives and rebuilds the rest from MonoCode's own markup.

Vendored from MonoCode, in web/mono/ (import paths adjusted):
  - icons.tsx                     src/shared/ui/icons.tsx
  - Popover.tsx, popover.ts,      src/shared/ui/Popover.tsx, src/shared/lib/popover.ts,
    layers.ts, NativePopupHost,   src/shared/lib/layers.ts, src/shared/ui/NativePopupHost.tsx,
    GlassBackdrop.tsx             src/app/shell/GlassBackdrop.tsx
  - Modal.tsx, useLockOverscroll  src/shared/ui/Modal.tsx, src/shared/hooks/useLockOverscroll.ts
  - PaneHeader.tsx                src/shared/ui/PaneHeader.tsx
  - SecondaryButton.tsx           src/shared/ui/SecondaryButton.tsx
  - Shimmer.tsx, TabLabel.tsx     src/shared/ui/Shimmer.tsx, src/shared/ui/TabLabel.tsx
  - TerminalSpinner.tsx           src/features/sessions/ui/TerminalSpinner.tsx
  - QuestionForm.tsx,             src/features/sessions/ui/QuestionForm.tsx,
    userQuestion.ts               src/features/sessions/model/userQuestion.ts
  - AccessPicker.tsx              src/features/sessions/ui/AccessPicker.tsx (modes mapped to
                                  AgentsCode's autonomy levels)
  - settings.tsx                  Toggle, Select, Segmented, Group and Row from
                                  src/features/settings/ui/SettingsView.tsx
  - ContextMeter.tsx              src/features/sessions/ui/ContextMeter.tsx (ring in the warning
                                  and danger tokens; the Compact now action left out)
  - RevealHeight.tsx              src/shared/ui/RevealHeight.tsx
  - TabWidthMotion.tsx,           src/app/shell/ClosingTab.tsx,
    useTabCloseMotion.ts,         src/features/workspace/hooks/useTabCloseMotion.ts (its settings
    motion.ts                     toggle left out), src/shared/lib/motion.ts (tabCloseDuration)
Vendored from MonoCode, elsewhere:
  - shared/contextUsage.ts        src/features/sessions/model/contextUsage.ts (its ContextUsage
                                  type moved to shared/types.ts)
Adapted from MonoCode markup:
  - web/styles.css                theme tokens and component styles from src/styles/index.css
  - web/panes/Transcript.tsx      the turn layout, rows and motion of AgentTranscript.tsx (phase
                                  groups, step arrival queue, prompt rise)
  - web/activity.ts               turn items, fold and work summaries from
                                  src/features/sessions/model/transcriptActivity.ts
  - web/ui/wordFade.ts            src/features/sessions/ui/wordFade.tsx (a stagger replaces its
                                  stream pacing, since engines here hand over whole blocks)
  - web/panes/Composer.tsx        Composer.tsx, ModelPicker's trigger, ToolButton, ComposerAction,
                                  and its attachment row, paste and drop handling, and its `/` and
                                  `@` picker keys
  - web/composer/Pickers.tsx      src/features/skills/ui/SkillPicker.tsx (its create-skill form left
                                  out), src/features/sessions/ui/FileMentionPicker.tsx and
                                  src/shared/ui/MatchText.tsx
  - web/composer/tokens.ts        src/shared/lib/fuzzy.ts, src/features/skills/model/slashCommands.ts,
                                  and the token and ranking parts of
                                  src/features/files/model/fileMentions.ts and fileIndex.ts
  - shared/composer.ts            injectSkillPrompt from src/features/skills/model/skills.ts
  - server/skills.ts              the skill catalog of src/features/skills/model/skills.ts, read from
                                  where Claude Code and Codex keep skills and commands
  - web/panes/ImageViews.tsx      AttachmentChip.tsx and the ImageLightbox it opens
  - web/App.tsx                   the inset layout and TitleBar tabs
  - web/assets/claude.svg, codex.svg   provider logos

